From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:45:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 034/342] WebPTranslator: identify WebP files shorter than 256
 bytes

DerivedIdentify() read a fixed 256 byte header and gave up when the
file was shorter, which small lossless (VP8L) images are.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/add-ons/translators/webp/WebPTranslator.cpp | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/translators/webp/WebPTranslator.cpp b/src/add-ons/translators/webp/WebPTranslator.cpp
index 54447049c5..6eb5e9b22c 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/translators/webp/WebPTranslator.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/translators/webp/WebPTranslator.cpp
@@ -137,10 +137,13 @@ WebPTranslator::DerivedIdentify(BPositionIO* stream,
 	if (outType != B_TRANSLATOR_BITMAP)
 		return B_NO_TRANSLATOR;
 
-	// Read header and first chunck bytes...
+	// Read header and first chunck bytes (a small lossless image can be
+	// shorter than the buffer)...
 	uint32 buf[64];
-	ssize_t size = sizeof(buf);
-	if (stream->Read(buf, size) != size)
+	ssize_t size = stream->Read(buf, sizeof(buf));
+	if (size < 0)
+		return size;
+	if (size < 16)
 		return B_IO_ERROR;
 
 	// Check it's a valid WebP format
